sentences.l:
But he lay on an island, suffering harsh pains,
in holy Lemnos, where the sons of the Achaeans left him,
toiling with an evil wound from a baleful-minded water-snake;

But he among the curved, sea-crossing ships
lay, withdrawn in wrath at Agamemnon, shepherd of the people,
Atreus’-son;

but the people beside the surf-line of the sea
with discuses were taking delight, and with javelins throwing,
and with bows;

and the horses beside their own chariots, each one,
eating lotus and marsh-nurtured celery,
stood;
